[E0303] Error: cannot apply `+=` to `i64` and `f64`
   ╭─[ err/85_compound_assignment_types/main.wip:6:11 ]
   │
 6 │     count += 1.5                // operands of different types
   │     ──┬── ─┬ ─┬─
   │       ╰─────────── `i64`
   │            │  │
   │            ╰────── operands of different types
   │               │
   │               ╰─── `f64`
   │
   │ Help: write it where `count` is declared: `var count: f64 = …`
   │
   │ Note 1: an integer is made a float, and a float an integer, by `as`, which may round
   │
   │ Note 2: `count` is `i64`, its literal's own: a variable of a number literal takes its type from its first use, where that says one
───╯
